{"name":"Honey Lime Chicken","hex":"#ddccbb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"honey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sweet, viscous, gold-colored fluid produced from plant nectar by bees, and often consumed by humans.","A variety of this substance."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Involving or resembling honey.","Of a pale yellow to brownish-yellow color, like most types of honey."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honey"},{"term":"lime","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any inorganic material containing calcium, usually calcium oxide (quicklime) or calcium hydroxide (slaked lime).","Any gluey or adhesive substance that traps or captures; sometimes a synonym for birdlime."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To treat with calcium hydroxide or calcium oxide (lime).","To smear with birdlime.\n To ensnare, catch, entrap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lime"},{"term":"chicken","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A domesticated subspecies of red junglefowl (Gallus gallus domesticus).","The meat from this bird eaten as food."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cowardly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chicken"}],"entries":[{"title":"Honey","blocks":[{"text":"Honey is a sweet and viscous substance made by several species of bees, the best-known of which are honey bees. Honey is made and stored to nourish bee colonies. Bees produce honey by gathering and then refining the sugary secretions of plants or the secretions of other insects, like the honeydew of aphids. This refinement takes place both within individual bees, through regurgitation and enzymatic activity, and during storage in the hive, through water evaporation that concentrates the honey's sugars until it is thick and viscous."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Runny_hunny.jpg/330px-Runny_hunny.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honey","wikidata":"Q10987"},{"title":"Chicken","blocks":[{"text":"The chicken is the domesticated form of the red junglefowl, originally native to Southeast Asia. It was first domesticated around 8,000 years ago and is one of the most common and widespread domesticated animals in the world. Chickens are primarily kept for their meat and eggs, though they are also kept as pets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Male_and_female_chicken_sitting_together.jpg/330px-Male_and_female_chicken_sitting_together.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicken","wikidata":"Q780"},{"title":"Lime (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lime is a color that is a shade of yellow-green, so named because it is a representation of the color of the citrus fruit lime. It is the color that is in between the web color chartreuse and yellow on the color wheel. Alternate names for this color included yellow-green, lemon-lime, lime green, or bitter lime."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg/330px-AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lime_(color)","wikidata":"Q906936"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Miels_d%27Alsace_agriculture_biologique.jpg/500px-Miels_d%27Alsace_agriculture_biologique.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Miels_d%27Alsace_agriculture_biologique.jpg/1280px-Miels_d%27Alsace_agriculture_biologique.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Miels_d%27Alsace_agriculture_biologique.jpg/500px-Miels_d%27Alsace_agriculture_biologique.jpg?utm_sour